cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "flexiv_control: a unified execution & safety layer for Flexiv Rizon arms"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Zihao
    family-names: Lu
    alias: ZihaoLu001
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZihaoLu001/flexiv_control"
url: "https://github.com/ZihaoLu001/flexiv_control"
abstract: >-
  A thin, real-time execution-and-safety layer between a high-level decision
  maker (policy, MPC planner, or teleoperator) and a Flexiv Rizon arm. It
  defines one action contract (Cartesian/joint chunks and deltas) used across
  teleoperation, model-predictive control, reinforcement learning, and
  real-to-sim-to-real manipulation, with a first-class safety supervisor, a
  backend switch for real hardware / a dependency-free simulator / MuJoCo, an
  optional cross-process server and client, a Gymnasium environment, a LeRobot
  adapter, an optional C++ 1 kHz real-time daemon, and an optional ROS 2
  overlay. Community project; not affiliated with Flexiv Robotics.
keywords:
  - robotics
  - manipulation
  - Flexiv Rizon
  - robot controller
  - reinforcement learning
  - model predictive control
  - teleoperation
  - real2sim2real
  - LeRobot
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.2.3
